  "title": "# Build: amberx-approvals-fix (Opus, high thinking; NO Fable on this account) · URGENT **Name:** Am…",
  "asked": "# Build: amberx-approvals-fix (Opus, high thinking; NO Fable on this account) · URGENT **Name:** AmberX approvals fix · **Category:** Fix ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"Why isn't AmberX launching approvals on my phone? It used to always pop up approvals.\" Three test approvals were sent ('TEST', 'TEST 2', 'TEST 3', harmless `date` runs): \"Nope, only when I open AmberX, and it says 'web page not available' in the approval waiting dialog.\" ... (Queue a fix?) \"Yep.\" Two bugs: 1. **No pop-up/notification when AmberX isn't open**: held/veto axHub approvals used to push to the phone and pop up; now nothing arrives until the app is opened. 2. **The approval waiting dialog in AmberX shows 'Web page not available'** instead of the approval page. Probably the same root cause as the sad face inside Molly (frame-ancestors/CSP on axHub's approval pages: the live hub allowed `patches.amberxai.com amberx.amberxai.com`, and Patches was retired; env `AXHUB_APPROVALS_FRAME_ANCESTORS` / `AXHUB_EMBED_FRAME_ANCESTORS`), or a WebView URL/host/SSL/cookie problem. **Find the real cause** on the live system (axHub container logs, the URL AmberX loads, the response headers) and write it in the report. Book to a free named agent. Plan Studio plan for it. Android work is an approved exception (Brett asked). ## Do - **Never a dead page**: the approval dialog in AmberX (and Molly, and the console's Follow Amber pop-up) renders **native Approve / Deny buttons** with the title, plain description, the exact call (folded) and the countdown, from the hub's approval feed/API. The embedded hub page is optional; if the frame/WebView fails, fall back to native buttons + 'Open in axHub' automatically, never 'web page not available' or a sad face. - Fix the frame/CSP config on axHub so the AmberX, Molly and console origins can load the approval page (axHub repo MossesX/axHub PR and/or its deploy env); remove the retired patches origin. - **Push**: find why approvals stopped notifying when the app is in the background or closed (FCM/web-push/ntfy registration, expired tokens, foreground service killed, notification channel disabled, battery optimisation, app updated without re-registering). Fix it, re-register the device automatically on app start, and add a **'Send test approval'** button in AmberX Settings plus a Systems-check row 'Phone gets approvals' with Auto fix. - A high-priority notification with Approve/Deny action buttons right on the notification where Android allows it; tapping opens the native dialog. - If an APK change is required, build it via CI, publish to axHub's app catalog (download stays at axhub.amberxai.com/apps/download/amberx-droid/latest) and notify Brett to install it. - Note: Brett also hit 'no such app file' on that download link tonight. Check the catalog vs files and fix it if broken. - Tests (fallback when the frame fails, approve/deny round trip, push registration), phone UI Review shots. PRs **through the merge queue only**. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned…",
